WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
Coins drop into a slot marked: Poor rate.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.260
Follow them down the pipes.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:10.150
They flow to a prison, a treadmill,
and a workhouse with a high wall.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.060
At the workhouse, separate
doors: men, women, children.

5
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.750
Asked to give at Christmas, Scrooge
points to what he already pays for.

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.110
"Are there no prisons?"

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.420
asked Scrooge.

8
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.990
He pays his share.

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.410
So why isn't that enough for Dickens?

10
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.820
In this mission, you'll uncover
the New Poor Law of 1834,

11
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.860
and a workhouse life kept no
better than the poorest labourer's.

12
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.450
And you'll weigh the places Scrooge names,

13
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.480
from prisons to the Union workhouses,
and ask what that list reveals.

14
00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:47.410
Your mission: explain why paying
his taxes isn't enough for Dickens.
